[{:db/id 17592186386696 :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ to $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124497 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0e4c9378-b054-5da6-b199-f46a138a46d3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0e4c9378-b054-5da6-b199-f46a138a46d3" :question/id #uuid "0e4c9378-b054-5da6-b199-f46a138a46d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-113603" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[x]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 4-6\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c1014636-1510-50f6-b488-e3fe8d24c13d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c1014636-1510-50f6-b488-e3fe8d24c13d" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1014636-1510-50f6-b488-e3fe8d24c13d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5c39bc95-ae02-5c17-9a57-15db094b94c3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-426822c2-147e-581d-8735-96a3bffe8321" "answer-5c39bc95-ae02-5c17-9a57-15db094b94c3" "answer-ef9b888d-cda8-5e1c-bef9-2a98c4f74288" "answer-89f6cf40-819f-5c6b-aeaf-667b443a0b60" "answer-e55ca324-fff5-5f74-ad7a-3c6af6f7f1cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-426822c2-147e-581d-8735-96a3bffe8321" :answer/id #uuid "426822c2-147e-581d-8735-96a3bffe8321" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c39bc95-ae02-5c17-9a57-15db094b94c3" :answer/id #uuid "5c39bc95-ae02-5c17-9a57-15db094b94c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef9b888d-cda8-5e1c-bef9-2a98c4f74288" :answer/id #uuid "ef9b888d-cda8-5e1c-bef9-2a98c4f74288" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-22 \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89f6cf40-819f-5c6b-aeaf-667b443a0b60" :answer/id #uuid "89f6cf40-819f-5c6b-aeaf-667b443a0b60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e55ca324-fff5-5f74-ad7a-3c6af6f7f1cd" :answer/id #uuid "e55ca324-fff5-5f74-ad7a-3c6af6f7f1cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}36 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124577 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8d0458bf-0ded-5bc5-82a5-015d07a4533d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8d0458bf-0ded-5bc5-82a5-015d07a4533d" :question/id #uuid "8d0458bf-0ded-5bc5-82a5-015d07a4533d" :question/math-academy-id "q-113615" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,C=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $C$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is a matrix whose columns are the vectors of $C$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-54566980-7132-5fea-9868-d89904943d38"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-54566980-7132-5fea-9868-d89904943d38" :answer-field/id #uuid "54566980-7132-5fea-9868-d89904943d38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4ef4749a-0f85-5a2d-a5e3-df28976db7b9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a95465bd-ca1b-539b-b564-dc5450e2c673" "answer-4ef4749a-0f85-5a2d-a5e3-df28976db7b9" "answer-75556eec-854e-532d-9072-0581f7715993" "answer-d0811b3a-bd66-51ab-9df6-b54f8983cb5f" "answer-d3c4b9b8-c843-5d6e-98b0-ea1b8a725222"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a95465bd-ca1b-539b-b564-dc5450e2c673" :answer/id #uuid "a95465bd-ca1b-539b-b564-dc5450e2c673" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ef4749a-0f85-5a2d-a5e3-df28976db7b9" :answer/id #uuid "4ef4749a-0f85-5a2d-a5e3-df28976db7b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75556eec-854e-532d-9072-0581f7715993" :answer/id #uuid "75556eec-854e-532d-9072-0581f7715993" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0811b3a-bd66-51ab-9df6-b54f8983cb5f" :answer/id #uuid "d0811b3a-bd66-51ab-9df6-b54f8983cb5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3c4b9b8-c843-5d6e-98b0-ea1b8a725222" :answer/id #uuid "d3c4b9b8-c843-5d6e-98b0-ea1b8a725222" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3b5b7055-d6b7-5899-a741-daa60aef491a" :activity/id #uuid "3b5b7055-d6b7-5899-a741-daa60aef491a" :activity/title "Changing a Basis Using the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048769 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-a2ad54ea-289c-5268-9e48-3009985055d0" "step-4de2c56b-39c0-5e14-a7fb-e708db903e6f" "step-4f40a8b0-4293-52f4-8c95-85c75998d506" "step-77dfbfe9-ef7f-5713-be40-7bce1749b9a7" "step-f5e3b29d-0add-527d-a99b-25156b6317ea"] :activity/first-step "step-a2ad54ea-289c-5268-9e48-3009985055d0" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-a2ad54ea-289c-5268-9e48-3009985055d0" :step/id #uuid "a2ad54ea-289c-5268-9e48-3009985055d0" :step/content 17592186323807 :step/next "step-4de2c56b-39c0-5e14-a7fb-e708db903e6f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4de2c56b-39c0-5e14-a7fb-e708db903e6f" :step/id #uuid "4de2c56b-39c0-5e14-a7fb-e708db903e6f" :step/content 17592186386696 :step/next "step-4f40a8b0-4293-52f4-8c95-85c75998d506" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4f40a8b0-4293-52f4-8c95-85c75998d506" :step/id #uuid "4f40a8b0-4293-52f4-8c95-85c75998d506" :step/content "question-0e4c9378-b054-5da6-b199-f46a138a46d3" :step/next "step-77dfbfe9-ef7f-5713-be40-7bce1749b9a7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-77dfbfe9-ef7f-5713-be40-7bce1749b9a7" :step/id #uuid "77dfbfe9-ef7f-5713-be40-7bce1749b9a7" :step/content 17592186247379 :step/next "step-f5e3b29d-0add-527d-a99b-25156b6317ea" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f5e3b29d-0add-527d-a99b-25156b6317ea" :step/id #uuid "f5e3b29d-0add-527d-a99b-25156b6317ea" :step/content "question-8d0458bf-0ded-5bc5-82a5-015d07a4533d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
